  "gate_should_answer": false,
  "pre_gate_answer": "# Briefing: City of Hartford MERF RFP Section 2 Minimum Requirements\n\n## Bottom Line\nThe provided evidence is **insufficient** to reliably list **all** minimum requirements in **Section 2 (pages 4–5)** of the **City of Hartford MERF general investment consultant RFP**.\n\n## What the Evidence Shows\nThe retrieved material **does not include** the actual Hartford MERF Section 2 text. Instead, it contains minimum requirement sections from other entities’ RFPs, including:\n\n- **SDCERS** General Investment Consultant RFP\n- **TMRS** Non-Discretionary General Investment Consulting Services RFP\n- **COAERS** General Investment Consultant RFP\n- **Arizona PSPRS** Non-Discretionary Investment Consultant Services RFP\n\nThese are **not interchangeable** with the Hartford MERF RFP and should not be used to reconstruct Hartford’s exact Section 2 requirements.\n\n## Why the Query Cannot Be Fully Answered\nYour question asks for **all minimum requirements** in a **specific section and page range** of a **specific Hartford RFP**. Because the underlying Hartford pages are missing, any complete answer would risk:\n\n- relying on **unsupported summary text**\n- **mixing in requirements** from unrelated RFPs\n- presenting an **incomplete or inaccurate** list\n\n## Hartford-Specific Claims Found in the Evidence\nThe only Hartford-specific-looking content in the evidence is an **unsupported prior summary** claiming that Section 2 includes:\n\n- **SEC registration** as an investment advisor under the **Investment Advisers Act of 1940**\n- **Minimum insurance coverage**, or application for such coverage by the proposal submission date:\n  - **General Liability:** $5,000,000\n  - **Errors and Omissions / Professional Liability:** $5,000,000\n  - **Fiduciary Liability:** $1,000,000\n  - **Workers’ Compensation and Employer’s Liability:** $1,000,000\n  - **Cybersecurity Coverage:** $1,000,000\n- The **City Treasurer’s Office** reserves the right to require **higher insurance coverage**\n- All minimum qualifications must be met by **March 15, 2024, 5:00 p.m. ET**\n- **Appendix A: Minimum Qualification Certification** must be completed\n- Failure to satisfy each minimum qualification results in **immediate rejection**\n\n## Reliability Assessment\nThese Hartford-specific points **cannot be verified** from the supplied evidence because the actual **Hartford MERF RFP pages 4–5 are not present**. Therefore, they should be treated as **unconfirmed** rather than as a definitive list.\n\n## Conclusion\nBased on the provided evidence, I **cannot accurately provide all minimum requirements** in Section 2 (pages 4–5) of the City of Hartford MERF general investment consultant RFP.\n\n## Recommended Next Step\nIf you provide the **Hartford MERF RFP** or specifically **pages 4–5**, I can extract and list **every minimum requirement precisely**.",
